  "synthesis": {
    "description": "Credit and desk leads tell the real-time traders when a counterparty is cut off or cleared to trade again, in short all-desk notices, and the risk side asks for or confirms credit reserves on named transactions. A reserve request is forwarded with the deal details below it, and the reply states how origination was split between the trader and the credit reserve, with any balance taken from the trader's origination that night.",
    "steps": [
      "Credit decides a counterparty is restricted or cleared, or a transaction needs a reserve.",
      "The desk lead sends a notice to the real-time group naming the counterparty and whether trading is allowed.",
      "Risk forwards the transaction details and asks for a credit reserve to be taken.",
      "The reserve and origination split is booked and confirmed back to the trader.",
      "Any shortfall in the split is corrected by moving origination from the trader's book."
    ],
    "approach": "Keep a single counterparty credit status list that the deal-entry system checks before a trade is booked, and have a reserve request form that captures the deal numbers and the split between trader origination and credit reserve, so the booking and confirmation come from one record instead of free-text email.",
    "rationale": "The rounds are short notices and reserve requests; a standard notice and reserve-request message with fixed fields (counterparty, status, effective time, deal numbers, reserve amount, split) would remove ambiguity and the rework seen when a split is corrected afterwards.",
    "artifact_type": "email_template"
  },
